BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (Message-Passing Graph Neural Networks for Molecular Solubility Prediction: A) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Synthetic Study) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Lucia Ferrero, Ibrahim Haddad, and Wenjun Zhao) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Synthetic Molecular Informatics Lab. All content is fictional and produced) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (solely as a retrieval evaluation fixture.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Abstract) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Aqueous solubility is a key determinant of drug-likeness, and graph neural) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (networks are natural candidates for predicting it from molecular structure.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (This synthetic study introduces the MolAnchor fingerprint and the AquaSol-9) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (dataset, and evaluates shallow message-passing architectures for solubility) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (regression. Our MolAnchor-GNN achieves a mean absolute error of 0.214 logS) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (units on the AquaSol-9 benchmark.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (1 Introduction) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Predicting aqueous solubility from molecular graphs is a standard benchmark) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (task in molecular machine learning. Molecules map naturally onto graphs, with) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (atoms as nodes and bonds as edges, which makes message-passing graph neural) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (networks a default modelling choice.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (This study is organized as follows. Section 2 introduces the AquaSol-9 dataset) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (and the MolAnchor fingerprint. Section 3 describes the model architecture,) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Section 4 reports results, and Sections 5 and 6 discuss limitations and) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (conclusions.) Tj T* ET
