BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (5 Limitations) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (AquaSol-9 is synthetic, so absolute errors do not transfer to experimental) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (solubility databases. The scaffold split is the only split we study, and we do) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (not compare against three-dimensional conformer-based models. MolAnchor) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (anchors require two-hop neighbourhood materialization, which is memory-heavy) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (for dense graphs.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (6 Conclusions) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Shallow message-passing networks with learned anchor fingerprints are strong) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (solubility predictors in controlled settings. On AquaSol-9, the four-layer) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (MolAnchor-GNN reaches 0.214 MAE, improving 14.1% over the strongest baseline) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (while avoiding the depth-saturation failure mode documented in graph-learning) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (surveys. Future work will extend anchors to longer ranges and evaluate on) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (public solubility benchmarks.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (References) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf ([1] L. Ferrero and W. Zhao. Anchor embeddings for molecular graphs. Journal of) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Synthetic Molecular Informatics, 2026. Fictional reference.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf ([2] I. Haddad. Controlled solubility benchmarks. Synthetic Workshop on) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Molecular Property Prediction, 2025. Fictional reference.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf ([3] A. Corvin and M. Okafor. Depth limits of message passing. Journal of) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Synthetic Graph Learning, 2025. Fictional reference.) Tj T* ET
